-- Row il-69. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound references kept beside the items. They pass.
-- Each control is a provision whose target is amended and still in force (I1) or not named by the repealing instruction (I2) on the instruments read.
-- The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in jt69-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the statuses there.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- I1 control: the replacement words cite subsection (a) of section 23, which item (8)(a) of SH 2274 amends and does not repeal.
#ASSERT `the provision is in force` `section 23(a)`
#ASSERT NOT (`the provision is repealed` `section 23(a)`)
#ASSERT map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `its label`) (`the provisions the words cite` "סעיף" (`item I1: the instruction of 2011`'s `the words it puts in place`) `the provisions item I1 can cite`) EQUALS LIST "section 23(a)"
#ASSERT all `the provision is in force` (`the provisions the words cite` "סעיף" (`item I1: the instruction of 2011`'s `the words it puts in place`) `the provisions item I1 can cite`)

-- I2 control: section 42, cited by paragraph (2) right after the paragraph of item I2, is in force on 2027-01-01 as the instruments read give it.
#ASSERT `the provision is in force` `section 42`
#ASSERT `the provision is in force on` `section 42` (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the section the reference cites is in force on` `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42` (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42`'s `the number of the section cited` EQUALS 42

-- The day a change took effect is not given by the pages read, so there is no answer, for the control and for the targets.
#ASSERT `the day the change to the provision took effect` `section 42` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the change to the provision took effect` `section 23(a)` EQUALS NOTHING
